export const GAME_FACTS = "GAME FACTS (the only things the Oracle knows)\nCosmic Ascension is a neon arcade space climber for Android and iPhone by QuantaCore Labs. The pilot climbs upward from platform to platform; altitude is measured in metres. Each sector ends at its Source: reach it to clear the sector.\n\nCONTROLS\nSteer left and right with the left and right halves of the screen (keyboard: A/D or arrow keys). Landing on a platform bounces you up automatically; there is no jump button. Bouncy platforms launch you 1.5 times higher.\nDash (the up-arrow button; keyboard Space or Enter): a straight-up burst, only when the dash meter is full; it refills faster while rising, and Dash Battery upgrades refill it faster.\nSuper Boost (the red lightning button; keyboard Shift): a huge upward blast with a 25 second cooldown.\nBoost Stars give a short boost; Mega Stars give a long one and count as 5 stars. While boosting you are safe from supernova flares and you shatter pulse mines.\n\nHOW A RUN ENDS AND HOW TO WIN\nA run ends when you fall off the bottom of the screen, or touch the Leviathan, a red pulse mine or a burning supernova flare. Saves, in order: the Cosmic Shield upgrade, the Second Wind anomaly (once per run) and the Prestige 4 Solar Sentinel chance.\nClearing a sector means reaching its Source altitude. Each sector has 3 mastery stars on the Star Map: Clear (reach the Source), Momentum (a long chain in that sector) and Swift (clear it fast).\n\nSECTORS (17)\n1. The Exosphere: the Source is at 10,000 m; needs pilot level 2.\n2. Crimson Nebula: the Source is at 28,000 m; needs pilot level 5.\n3. Void Horizon: the Source is at 45,000 m; needs pilot level 9.\n4. Astral Abyss: the Source is at 62,000 m; needs pilot level 12.\n5. Quantum Rift: the Source is at 80,000 m; needs pilot level 16.\n6. Celestial Gateway: the Source is at 98,000 m; needs pilot level 19.\n7. Supernova Core: the Source is at 115,000 m; needs pilot level 23.\n8. Dimensional Tear: the Source is at 132,000 m; needs pilot level 26.\n9. The Source: the Source is at 150,000 m; needs pilot level 30.\n10. Nebula Void: The Awakening: the Source is at 200,000 m; needs pilot level 40; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n11. Nebula Void: Celestial Expanse: the Source is at 245,000 m; needs pilot level 49; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n12. Nebula Void: Edge of Time: the Source is at 285,000 m; needs pilot level 57; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n13. Nebula Void: The Singularity: the Source is at 330,000 m; needs pilot level 66; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n14. Abyssal Dimension: Tartarus: the Source is at 370,000 m; needs pilot level 74; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n15. Abyssal Dimension: Elysium: the Source is at 415,000 m; needs pilot level 83; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n16. Nebula Void: Omniverse: the Source is at 455,000 m; needs pilot level 91; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n17. The True Void: the Source is at 500,000 m; needs pilot level 100; premium sector (bought in the Void Emporium).\n\nSECTOR LAWS (each early sector teaches one law; later sectors mix them; rifts get two)\nLaw I ASCENT (first met in The Exosphere): Land dead-centre for a PERFECT. Chain them to multiply shards and trigger Momentum Surges.\nLaw II DRIFT (first met in Crimson Nebula): Platforms slide on invisible tides. Time your fall to meet them.\nLaw III DECAY (first met in Void Horizon): Cracked platforms hold exactly once, then crumble into the dark.\nLaw IV PHASE (first met in Astral Abyss): Phase platforms blink between worlds. They flicker just before they vanish.\nLaw V CONTINUITY (first met in Quantum Rift): The walls are gone. Leave one edge and you return from the other.\nLaw VI CURRENTS (first met in Celestial Gateway): Solar winds push you sideways inside their bands. Lean into them.\nLaw VII PULSE (first met in Supernova Core): Red pulse mines drift in the dark. Touch one and you are gone — but a boost shatters them.\nLaw VIII GRAVITY WELLS (first met in Dimensional Tear): Collapsed stars pull everything near them. Use the pull to slingshot.\nLaw IX CONVERGENCE (first met in The Source): Every law at once. The Source tests everything the void has taught you.\n\nMOMENTUM CHAIN\nLanding near the centre of a platform is a PERFECT (the centre band is 20% of the platform's width, at least 9 px). Each PERFECT grows the chain; a sloppy landing resets it to 0. Every 3 perfects raise the tier, up to tier 4, and shards are worth 1 + tier times as much (up to x5). Every 5th perfect fires a Momentum Surge that launches you higher. Landing on the same platform again neither grows nor breaks the chain.\n\nANOMALY GATES AND ANOMALIES\nAnomaly Gates appear at 1,000 m, 3,000 m, 6,000 m, 10,000 m, 15,000 m and so on (at most 8 per run). At each gate you draft one anomaly for the rest of the run:\nCommon: Featherfall (Gravity is 12% weaker); Magnetar (Your pickup magnet reaches 140px further); Star Forge (Boost stars appear 60% more often); Wide Stance (New platforms are 20% wider); Afterburner (Star and mega boosts last 50% longer); Slingshot (Bouncy platforms launch you 20% harder); Cryo Core (Super Boost recharges 40% faster); Greed Field (Twice as many shards spawn); Precision Lens (The PERFECT zone is 40% wider); Storm Anchor (Currents and gravity wells pull you 50% less).\nRare: Overcharge (Every PERFECT landing fully recharges your dash); Chain Reactor (Momentum tiers climb every 2 perfects instead of 3); Phase Shift (Dashing makes you untouchable to mines and flares for 1 second); Wormhole Tuner (Wormholes appear twice as often); Momentum Lock (A sloppy landing halves your chain instead of breaking it); Leviathan Bane (The Leviathan is 25% slower and solar flares warn 50% longer).\nEpic: Glass Cannon (Double shards from every pickup. Pulse mines grow 40% larger); Second Wind (The first fatal fall this run launches you back up instead); Void Walker (The walls wrap for the rest of this run (Law of Continuity)); Surge Engine (Momentum Surge fires every 4th perfect and launches harder).\n\nUPGRADES (Void Emporium, Tech tab; each level costs more)\nEngine Power (max level 20, from 500 shards): Increases boost force.\nCoin Magnet (max level 15, from 1,000 shards): Increases coin collection radius.\nDash Battery (max level 10, from 750 shards): Increases max dash charge.\nPlasma Thrusters (max level 15, from 2,500 shards): Adds passive upward lift.\nProbability Matrix (max level 10, from 5,000 shards): Better power-up spawns.\nHyper Velocity (max level 10, from 10,000 shards): Sharper steering: +3% lateral thrust per level.\nGravity Resistor (max level 10, from 8,000 shards): Reduces gravitational pull.\nCoin Multiplier (max level 10, from 25,000 shards): Increases coin value.\nCosmic Shield (max level 5, premium, bought with real money): Absorbs 1 fatal hit per run.\nOffline Earnings (max level 10, premium, bought with real money): Earns coins while closed.\nRift Walker (max level 5, premium, bought with real money): Increases special spawns.\nTime Dilation (max level 5, premium, bought with real money): Slows game speed scaling.\n\nHAZARDS AND EVENTS\nLeviathan: a rising beast that lasts 25 seconds; it only catches pilots who stall, so keep climbing. The Leviathan Bane anomaly and the Leviathan Slayer dark-matter upgrade slow it.\nSupernova: lasts 15 seconds, gravity is heavier and flare columns are telegraphed before they burn; move out of a warned column or be boosting.\nWormholes: touch one to jump 300 m upward at once.\nPulse mines (Law VII) kill on touch unless you are boosting. Gravity wells (Law VIII) pull you in; use them to slingshot. Cracked platforms (Law III) hold once.\n\nCURRENCIES\nShards: the main currency, collected while climbing, spent on upgrades, skins, trails and pilots. The Coin Multiplier upgrade and the Momentum Chain raise their value.\nStars: Boost Stars count 1, Mega Stars count 5.\nXP raises your pilot level, which unlocks sectors.\nDark Matter: earned by Cosmic Collapse (prestige), about 1 per 5,000 m of your best altitude; it buys permanent upgrades (Leviathan Slayer, Supernova Greed, Dark Wealth).\n\nPRESTIGE (Cosmic Collapse)\nAvailable at pilot level 100. It resets shards, level, XP, high score and the shard-bought upgrades (premium upgrades stay), grants Dark Matter and a permanent rank:\nPrestige 1 Rift Walker: +5% Coin Magnet Range, Void Wings Badge.\nPrestige 2 Quantum Specter: -5% Gravity Force, Chrono Trail visual.\nPrestige 3 Nebula Weaver: +5% Shard Credits Values, Nebula Core Skin unlocked.\nPrestige 4 Solar Sentinel: +5% Damage Invincibility Save, Solar Corona Badge.\nPrestige 5 Void Voyager: +5% Jump Flight Thrust, Cyan Warp Flash jump style.\nPrestige 6 Chrono Overlord: +5% Horizontal Dash Impulse, Chrono Glass UI style.\nPrestige 7 Elysian Champion: +5% Offline Credits Value, Glowing Gold Elysian Halo.\nPrestige 8 Astral Deity: -5% Terminal Fall Speed, Sparks Engine Trail.\nPrestige 9 Singularity Master: +5% Pushback Control Resistance, Event Horizon Avatar.\nPrestige 10 Ascended Source: +10% XP & Shard Blessing, Rainbow Creator Aura.\n\nMODES AND FEATURES\nDaily Rift: one shared seeded course per day with three objectives; a Supernova at 3,000 m and the Leviathan at 7,000 m. The day changes at 4 pm Mountain Time.\nDaily Signal: log in each day for a 7-day reward cycle (day 1 500 shards + 50 XP, day 2 750 shards + 75 XP, day 3 1,000 shards + 100 XP, day 4 1,500 shards + 150 XP, day 5 2,000 shards + 200 XP, day 6 3,000 shards + 300 XP, day 7 5,000 shards + 750 XP); rewards scale up with your level and prestige; miss a day and the streak restarts.\nWeekly Ladder: a leaderboard of the best run this week (weeks start Monday).\nGhost racing: race up to 3 rival ghosts plus your own best run; turn ghosts on or off in Settings.\nChallenge Codes: a 7-character code (shown as ABC-DEFG) that shares a seeded course; friends race the same course.\nAscension Relay: one seeded course climbed by a chain of pilots. When you fall you hand off a Flight Card link and the next pilot starts at your altitude. The Source is 10,000 m, at most 8 legs, one Daily leg per pilot per day.\nGenerative Rift: describe a world and the void builds a solo rift with its own gravity, jump strength, bouncy platforms and colours.\nTrophy Vault: 34 trophies with shard and XP rewards, for example First Flight (Complete your first run); Stratosphere (Reach 1,000m in a single run); Thermosphere (Reach 5,000m in a single run); Exosphere (Reach 10,000m in a single run); Voidwalker (Reach 25,000m in a single run); Starborn (Reach 50,000m in a single run); Source Seeker (Reach 100,000m in a single run); Source Touched (Reach the Source of any sector); Sector Sweep (Reach the Source of 5 sectors); Wormhole Rider (Transit 10 wormholes); Wormhole Legend (Transit 100 wormholes); Mega Collector (Absorb 25 mega stars).\nSkins, trails and pilots: sold for shards or real money in the Void Emporium (Tech, Trails, Avatars and Void Series tabs). Skins are looks only.\nOffline Earnings (premium upgrade): earns shards while the app is closed, up to 24 hours.\n\nTIPS\nAim for the centre of every platform: perfects multiply shards and surges carry you up. Save the dash to rescue a bad fall. Use Super Boost to escape the Leviathan or cross a supernova. Buy Engine Power, Coin Magnet and Dash Battery early, then Coin Multiplier. Pick Second Wind or Wide Stance if you keep falling; pick Greed Field or Glass Cannon to farm shards. Learn each sector's law in the sector that introduces it before facing the mixed later sectors.";
